{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-43983","model_call":3,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ vogue inclusive audience)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ vogue inclusive audience)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_248113334#0_464876576","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q302","rank":1,"snippet":"s most cutting-edge fashion designers. When it comes to fashion, few people know the industry like Jaime Perlman. Formerly <cover>Vogue UK’s creative director, she’s now the founder and creative director of More or Less magazine. She was inspired to create an of-the-moment publication to advocate for a modern fashion industry built on planet-conscious creativity over cost and consumption. “I wanted to create a platform that celebrated fashion that was a bit more personal—something that was inclusive and celebrated style, and focused on designers who made sustainability a priority,” she says. To embody that ethos, Jaime has teamed up with Microsoft and four of fashion’s most innovative designers—Bethany Williams, Phoebe English, Fredrik Tjærandsen, and Rottingdean Bazaar—to reimagine the process of designing, creating, and showing garments. The initiative, Augmented Atelier, is an ambitious design premise and an alternate take on fashion. It offers new tools for waste-free collaborative design, as well as interactive online retail and customized try-ons, showcasing new applications of virtual-only garments to a global audience. </cover>YouTube Microsoft 767K subscribers Augmented Atelier, an innovative digital fashion showcase powered by Microsoft Azure Spatial Anchors Watch later Share Info"},"time":70},"model_calls":3,"document_judgments":0,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
